.TH TMV 1 "2026-11-05" "tmv 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmv \- treemap viewer for a process virtual address space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmv
[\fIPID\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmv
reads the virtual memory map of a running Linux process from
.IR /proc/\fIPID\fR
and renders the address space as a
.BR WizTree -style
treemap: every rectangle is a mapping, and its area is proportional to the
selected metric (virtual size, RSS, PSS, private, shared or swap).
.PP
Sampling is read-only and requires either the same user ID as the target or
.BR CAP_SYS_PTRACE .
Without \fBsmaps\fR permissions the viewer falls back to virtual sizes.
.PP
The interface is a full-screen TUI; press \fB?\fR for the key reference and
\fBq\fR to quit. Memory contents can be inspected with \fBx\fR, which reads from
.IR /proc/\fIPID\fR/mem .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \fIPID\fR
Target process ID. Required unless \fB\-\-demo\fR or \fB\-\-replay\fR is used.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Use synthetic data so the interface can be previewed without a Linux process.
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " FILE"
Replay a snapshot written by \fB\-\-json\fR or \fB\-\-save\-baseline\fR.
No sampling or process attachment takes place.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECONDS"
Auto-refresh interval; \fB0\fR (the default) refreshes only when
.B r
is pressed.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the snapshot as JSON and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-report
Print a text report and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
Number of entries in the report and diff lists (default \fB10\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " FILE"
Load a snapshot used as the comparison baseline.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-baseline " FILE"
Write the current snapshot to
.I FILE
as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-metric " METRIC"
Metric used for areas and diffs: \fBvirtual\fR, \fBrss\fR, \fBpss\fR,
\fBprivate\fR, \fBshared\fR or \fBswap\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-lookup " ADDR"
Resolve a hexadecimal address to module, symbol and source line, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-read " ADDR[:LEN]"
Read memory at a hexadecimal address and print it in
.BR xxd (1)
style, then exit. \fILEN\fR defaults to 256 bytes and is capped at 65536.
.TP
.B \-\-stack
Unwind the main thread and print symbolized frames, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-svg " FILE"
Render the address space to a self-contained SVG file and exit.  Every block
carries a hover tooltip (path, size, address range, permissions); with the
treemap layout, clicking a group zooms into it (inline JavaScript, no external
assets).
.TP
.BI \-\-svg\-format " FORMAT"
Layout used by \fB\-\-svg\fR: \fBtreemap\fR (default, drill-down) or
\fBflame\fR (horizontal icicle graph).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Do not read or write the configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B arrows, hjkl
Move the selection; in list view move row by row.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Esc
Descend into the selected block / go back one level.
.TP
.B v
Toggle between treemap and a flat mapping list.
.TP
.B f
Filter mappings by path, label or permissions (substring).
.TP
.B F
Filter mappings with a case-insensitive regular expression.
.TP
.B /
Resolve a hexadecimal address and jump to it.
.TP
.BR m ", " g ", " o
Cycle metric, grouping and sort order.
.TP
.BR p ", " t ", " a
Toggle page map, thread stacks and accounting panel.
.TP
.B x
Hex-dump the mapping under the cursor.
.TP
.B s
Open the settings panel.
.TP
.B r
Refresh once; press twice quickly to toggle auto-refresh.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tmv/config.toml
Interface preferences written on exit; override the location with
.BR TMV_CONFIG .
.TP
.I /proc/PID/maps, /proc/PID/smaps
Address space and per-mapping accounting.
.TP
.I /proc/PID/mem
Memory contents, used by \fBx\fR and \fB\-\-read\fR.
.TP
.I /proc/PID/pagemap
Page residency, requires \fBCAP_SYS_ADMIN\fR.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid command line argument.
.TP
.B 2
Process not found, or address without a symbol.
.TP
.B 3
Insufficient permissions.
.TP
.B 4
Other collection error, unsupported platform, or invalid snapshot file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tmv 4242
Inspect process 4242 interactively.
.TP
.B tmv 4242 \-\-report \-\-top 20
Print the twenty largest mappings.
.TP
.B tmv 4242 \-\-read 0x7f0000000000:128
Hex-dump 128 bytes at a given address.
.TP
.B tmv 4242 \-\-svg mem.svg
Export the treemap as an interactive SVG file.
.TP
.B tmv 4242 \-\-svg flame.svg \-\-svg\-format flame
Export the address space as a flame graph.
.TP
.B tmv 4242 \-\-svg diff.svg \-\-baseline base.json
Highlight growth and shrinkage against a saved baseline.
.TP
.B tmv \-\-demo
Preview the interface on a non-Linux host.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ps (1),
.BR proc (5),
.BR readelf (1),
.BR gdb (1)
